Description:
    Everything `rails generate resource` writes, with the route drawn by
    `recourses` rather than `resources`. That one word is what hands the model
    its seven screens: index, new, create, edit, update and destroy, served by
    this gem without a controller or a view of your own.

    The controller it writes inherits RecoursesController rather than
    ApplicationController, so the actions and the views arrive with it.

Example:
    bin/rails generate recourse contact name:string phone:string

    This will create:
        app/models/contact.rb, its migration, fixture and test
        app/controllers/contacts_controller.rb, inheriting RecoursesController
        app/helpers/contacts_helper.rb and app/views/contacts
        recourses :contacts, in config/routes.rb

    bin/rails generate recourse admin/market name:string

    This will draw the route inside `namespace :admin`.
